  "_comment": "VestaRV: the PINMUX pad menu. Per pad, the ordered list of functions its select codes 1..N reach; code 0 is always DISABLED and is not listed. This file is the generic, editable half of the pin mux: platform/common/python/mcu_vhd.py PINMUX_FN owns the RTL signal spelling and the output-enable policy of each function name, generate.py drops a function whose peripheral the configuration does not instantiate and COMPACTS the pad's menu, and peripherals.pinmuxPads says how many pads exist. The 19 rows below are the pad census of owner decision O12: pmx0-pmx18, PDUW16SDGZ_G 1.0 V bidirectional pads, west 6 / south 6 / east 1 / north 6, whose ring placement lives with the pad ring and not here. Each pad carries a mirror of one GPIO port bit plus one of four relocatable serial classes, so the 19 pads between them reach every relocatable function. A pad listed here beyond peripherals.pinmuxPads is ignored, and a pad short of it gets an empty menu and is permanently high-Z.",
